From d271da3d6fc78188e0c006ee780c84832c6a0e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:25:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/42] vk: optionally allocate uncached host visible memory as
 cached

Port of google/gfxstream e2ddfc73 (google/gfxstream#209,
ModAVD/ModAVD#37) in place of the local ANDROID_EMU_VK_WC_AS_CACHED
change, which picked a cached type per allocation in
on_vkAllocateMemory():

- Add the VulkanAllocateUncachedHostVisibleAsCached feature, off by
  default; the emulator decides whether it is on.
- With it, a guest memory type whose host memory type is host visible
  but neither cached nor device local maps to a HOST_VISIBLE |
  HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED type on the same heap, unless host
  visible memory is exported or imported (ExternalBlob, SystemBlob,
  VulkanAllocateHostVisibleAsUdmabuf, VulkanAllocateHostMemory).
- transformToGuestMemoryRequirements() goes through the guest memory
  types, so a resource that allows the original host type but not the
  replacement no longer sees that guest type. It skips the AHB type, as
  before.
- Imported ColorBuffer and Buffer memory keeps its memory type
  (upstream ececb7a2, the previous change).

FindReplacementCachedHostMemoryTypeIndex() and the unit tests are the
same as upstream. This tree keeps mGuestToHostMemoryTypeIndexMap where
upstream has a list of guest memory types, so the map is what changes.

Local diagnostics: one line for the first allocation from each guest
memory type that moves, and a rate-limited line when a resource loses a
guest memory type to the replacement.

Test: VkGuestMemoryUtilsTest.* 12/12; each of 8 mutations of the
      replacement lookup fails at least one case
Test: with the emulator turning the feature on (qemu "opengles:
      allocate uncached host visible memory as cached ..."), 10 Star
      Rail cold boots log the replacement and never "has no effect";
      Vulkan validation on Star Rail, Endfield and Arknights shows no
      new error category and no memory type or mapping error
Test: frame rate against 0.37 on Star Rail (2 A/B pairs) and Endfield
      (1 pair): no regression

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#37
